\b First Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, give us grace to cast away the works of\par
darkness, and put on the armor of light, now in the time of\par
this mortal life in which your Son Jesus Christ came to visit\par
us in great humility; that in the last day, when he shall come\par
again in his glorious majesty to judge both the living and the\par
dead, we may rise to the life immortal; through him who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Advent\i0\par
  \par
\b Second Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Merciful God, who sent your messengers the prophets to\par
preach repentance and prepare the way for our salvation:\par
Give us grace to heed their warnings and forsake our sins,\par
that we may greet with joy the coming of Jesus Christ our\par
Redeemer; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
 \par
Preface of Advent\i0\par
  \par
\b\par
Third Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Stir up your power, O Lord, and with great might come\par
among us; and, because we are sorely hindered by our sins,\par
let your bountiful grace and mercy speedily help and deliver\par
us; through Jesus Christ our Lord, to whom, with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, be honor and glory, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Advent\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional winter\par
Ember Days\i0 .\fs24\par
  \par
\b Fourth Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Purify our conscience, Almighty God, by your daily visitation,\par
that your Son Jesus Christ, at his coming, may find in us a\par
mansion prepared for himself; who lives and reigns with you,\par
in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Advent\i0\par
  \par
\b The Nativity of Our Lord:  Christmas Day\b0   \i\fs20 December 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you make us glad by the yearly festival of the birth\par
of your only Son Jesus Christ:  Grant that we, who joyfully\par
receive him as our Redeemer, may with sure confidence\par
behold him when he comes to be our Judge; who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you have caused this holy night to shine with the\par
brightness of the true Light:  Grant that we, who have known\par
the mystery of that Light on earth, may also enjoy him\par
perfectly in heaven; where with you and the Holy Spirit he\par
lives and reigns, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\i0\par
 \par
\i or this\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have given your only-begotten Son to\par
take our nature upon him, and to be born [this day] of a pure\par
virgin:  Grant that we, who have been born again and made\par
your children by adoption and grace, may daily be renewed\par
by your Holy Spirit; through our Lord Jesus Christ, to whom\par
with you and the same Spirit be honor and glory, now and\par
for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\fs20 The Collect immediately preceding and any of the sets of Proper Lessons\par
for Christmas Day serve for any weekdays between Holy Innocents\rquote  Day \par
and the First Sunday after Christmas Day.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\b First Sunday after Christmas Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 This Sunday takes precedence over the three Holy Days which follow\par
Christmas Day. As necessary, the observance of one, two, or all three\par
of them, is postponed one day.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have poured upon us the new light of\par
your incarnate Word:  Grant that this light, enkindled in our\par
hearts, may shine forth in our lives; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\par
 \i0  \par
\b The Holy Name\b0     \i\fs20 January 1\i0\fs24\par
 \par
Eternal Father, you gave to your incarnate Son the holy name\par
of Jesus to be the sign of our salvation:  Plant in every heart,\par
we pray, the love of him who is the Savior of the world, our\par
Lord Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
 \b Second Sunday after Christmas Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who wonderfully created, and yet more wonderfully\par
restored, the dignity of human nature:  Grant that we may\par
share the divine life of him who humbled himself to share\par
our humanity, your Son Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns\par
with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
 \par
\b The Epiphany\b0     \i\fs20 January 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, by the leading of a star you manifested your only Son\par
to the peoples of the earth:  Lead us, who know you now by\par
faith, to your presence, where we may see your glory face to\par
face; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 The preceding Collect, with the Psalm and Lessons for the Epiphany, or\par
those for the Second Sunday after Christmas, serves for weekdays\par
between the Epiphany and the following Sunday.  The Preface of the\par
Epiphany is used.\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\b First Sunday after the Epiphany:  The Baptism of our Lord\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Father in heaven, who at the baptism of Jesus in the River\par
Jordan proclaimed him your beloved Son and anointed him\par
with the Holy Spirit:  Grant that all who are baptized into his\par
Name may keep the covenant they have made, and boldly\par
confess him as Lord and Savior; who with you and the Holy\par
Spirit lives and reigns, one God, in glory everlasting. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
 \par
\b Second Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
 \par
Almighty God, whose Son our Savior Jesus Christ is the light\par
of the world:  Grant that your people, illumined by your Word\par
and Sacraments, may shine with the radiance of Christ's\par
glory, that he may be known, worshiped, and obeyed to the\par
ends of the earth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who with\par
you and the Holy Spirit lives and reigns, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Third Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Give us grace, O Lord, to answer readily the call of our\par
Savior Jesus Christ and proclaim to all people the Good News\par
of his salvation, that we and the whole world may perceive\par
the glory of his marvelous works; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Fourth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, you govern all things both in\par
heaven and on earth:  Mercifully hear the supplications of\par
your people, and in our time grant us your peace; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b Fifth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Set us free, O God, from the bondage of our sins, and give us\par
the liberty of that abundant life which you have made known\par
to us in your Son our Savior Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns\par
with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
\i0\par
\b Sixth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard O God, the strength of all who put their trust in you:\par
Mercifully accept our prayers; and because in our weakness\par
we can do nothing good without you, give us the help of your\par
grace, that in keeping your commandments we may please\par
you both in will and deed; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Seventh Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Lord, you have taught us that without love whatever we\par
do is worth nothing: Send your Holy Spirit and pour into our\par
hearts your greatest gift, which is love, the true bond of peace\par
and of all virtue, without which whoever lives is accounted\par
dead before you.  Grant this for the sake of your only Son\par
Jesus Christ, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Eighth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Most loving Father, whose will it is for us to give thanks for\par
all things, to fear nothing but the loss of you, and to cast all\par
\par
our care on you who care for us: Preserve us from faithless\par
fears and worldly anxieties, that no clouds of this mortal life\par
may hide from us the light of that love which is immortal,\par
and which you have manifested to us in your Son Jesus Christ\par
our Lord; who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Last Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 This Proper is always used on the Sunday before Ash Wednesday\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who before the passion of your only-begotten Son\par
revealed his glory upon the holy mountain: Grant to us that\par
we, beholding by faith the light of his countenance, may be\par
strengthened to bear our cross, and be changed into his\par
likeness from glory to glory; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\par
 \i0  \par
\b Ash Wednesday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 264.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, you hate nothing you have\par
made and forgive the sins of all who are penitent:  Create and\par
make in us new and contrite hearts, that we, worthily\par
lamenting our sins and acknowledging our wretchedness,\par
may obtain of you, the God of all mercy, perfect remission\par
and forgiveness; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Lent\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 This Collect, with the corresponding Psalm and Lessons, also serves for\par
the weekdays which follow, except as otherwise appointed\i0 .\b\fs24 First Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose blessed Son was led by the Spirit to be\par
tempted by Satan: Come quickly to help us who are assaulted\par
by many temptations; and, as you know the weaknesses of\par
each of us, let each one find you mighty to save; through\par
Jesus Christ your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Lent\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional spring\par
Ember Days.\fs24\par
 \i0\par
\b Second Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, whose glory it is always to have mercy:  Be gracious\par
to all who have gone astray from your ways, and bring them\par
again with penitent hearts and steadfast faith to embrace and\par
hold fast the unchangeable truth of your Word, Jesus Christ\par
your Son; who with you and the Holy Spirit lives and reigns,\par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of Lent \i0\par
 \par
\b Third Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you know that we have no power in ourselves\par
to help ourselves:  Keep us both outwardly in our bodies and\par
inwardly in our souls, that we may be defended from all\par
adversities which may happen to the body, and from all evil\par
thoughts which may assault and hurt the soul; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Lent\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b Fourth Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Gracious Father, whose blessed Son Jesus Christ came down\par
from heaven to be the true bread which gives life to the world:\par
Evermore give us this bread, that he may live in us, and we in\par
him; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Lent\i0\par
  \par
\b Fifth Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you alone can bring into order the unruly\par
wills and affections of sinners:  Grant your people grace to\par
love what you command and desire what you promise; that,\par
among the swift and varied changes of the world, our hearts\par
may surely there be fixed where true joys are to be found;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Lent\i0\par
  \par
\b Sunday of the Passion:  Palm Sunday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 270.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everliving God, in your tender love for the\par
human race you sent your Son our Savior Jesus Christ to\par
take upon him our nature, and to suffer death upon the cross,\par
giving us the example of his great humility:  Mercifully grant\par
that we may walk in the way of his suffering, and also share\par
in his resurrection; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\b Monday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose most dear Son went not up to joy but\par
first he suffered pain, and entered not into glory before he\par
was crucified:  Mercifully grant that we, walking in the way\par
of the cross, may find it none other than the way of life and\par
peace; through Jesus Christ your Son our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
 \par
\b Tuesday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, by the passion of your blessed Son you made an\par
instrument of shameful death to be for us the means of life:\par
Grant us so to glory in the cross of Christ, that we may gladly\par
suffer shame and loss for the sake of your Son our Savior\par
Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\par
 \i0  \par
\b Wednesday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord God, whose blessed Son our Savior gave his body to be\par
whipped and his face to be spit upon:  Give us grace to accept\par
joyfully the sufferings of the present time, confident of the\par
glory that shall be revealed; through Jesus Christ your Son our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\par
 \i0\par
\par
\b Maundy Thursday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 274.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty Father, whose dear Son, on the night before he\par
suffered, instituted the Sacrament of his Body and Blood:\par
Mercifully grant that we may receive it thankfully in\par
remembrance of Jesus Christ our Lord, who in these holy\par
mysteries gives us a pledge of eternal life; and who now lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\par
\i0  \par
\b Good Friday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 276.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, we pray you graciously to behold this your\par
family, for whom our Lord Jesus Christ was willing to be\par
betrayed, and given into the hands of sinners, and to suffer\par
death upon the cross; who now lives and reigns with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\par
\b Holy Saturday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 283.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard O God, Creator of heaven and earth: Grant that, as the\par
crucified body of your dear Son was laid in the tomb and\par
rested on this holy Sabbath, so we may await with him the\par
coming of the third day, and rise with him to newness of life;\par
who now lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever. \i Amen\i0 .\par
\par
\b\par
Easter Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 The Liturgy of the Easter Vigil is on page 285.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who for our redemption gave your only-begotten\par
Son to the death of the cross, and by his glorious resurrection\par
delivered us from the power of our enemy:  Grant us so to die\par
daily to sin, that we may evermore live with him in the joy of\par
his resurrection; through Jesus Christ your Son our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who made this most holy night to shine with the\par
glory of the Lord\rquote s resurrection:  Stir up in your Church that\par
Spirit of adoption which is given to us in Baptism, that we,\par
being renewed both in body and mind, may worship you in\par
sincerity and truth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever. \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\i\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Almighty God, who through your only-begotten Son Jesus\par
Christ overcame death and opened to us the gate of\par
everlasting life:  Grant that we, who celebrate with joy the\par
day of the Lord\rquote s resurrection, may be raised from the death\par
of sin by your life-giving Spirit; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
 \par
Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Monday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, we pray, Almighty God, that we who celebrate with\par
awe the Paschal feast may be found worthy to attain to\par
\par
everlasting joys; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
 \par
\b Tuesday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who by the glorious resurrection of your Son Jesus\par
Christ destroyed death and brought life and immortality to\par
light:  Grant that we, who have been raised with him, may\par
abide in his presence and rejoice in the hope of eternal glory;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, to whom, with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, be dominion and praise for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Wednesday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, whose blessed Son made himself known to his\par
disciples in the breaking of bread:  Open the eyes of our faith,\par
that we may behold him in all his redeeming work; who lives\par
and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Thursday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, who in the Paschal mystery\par
established the new covenant of reconciliation:  Grant that all\par
who have been reborn into the fellowship of Christ\rquote s Body\par
may show forth in their lives what they profess by their faith;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\par
 \i0  \par
\par
\b Friday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty Father, who gave your only Son to die for our sins\par
and to rise for our justification:  Give us grace so to put away\par
the leaven of malice and wickedness, that we may always\par
serve you in pureness of living and truth; through Jesus\par
Christ your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\par
 \i0  \par
\b Saturday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard We thank you, heavenly Father, that you have delivered us\par
from the dominion of sin and death and brought us into the\par
kingdom of your Son; and we pray that, as by his death he\par
has recalled us to life, so by his love he may raise us to eternal\par
joys; who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Second Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, who in the Paschal mystery\par
established the new covenant of reconciliation:  Grant that all\par
who have been reborn into the fellowship of Christ\rquote s Body\par
may show forth in their lives what they profess by their faith;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\par
 \i0  \par
\b Third Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, whose blessed Son made himself known to his\par
disciples in the breaking of bread:  Open the eyes of our faith,\par
that we may behold him in all his redeeming work; who lives\par
\par
and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Fourth Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, whose Son Jesus is the good shepherd of your people;\par
Grant that when we hear his voice we may know him who\par
calls us each by name, and follow where he leads; who, with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, lives and reigns, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
  \par
\b Fifth Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whom truly to know is everlasting life:  Grant\par
us so perfectly to know your Son Jesus Christ to be the way,\par
the truth, and the life, that we may steadfastly follow his\par
steps in the way that leads to eternal life; through Jesus Christ\par
your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
 \b\par
Sixth Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you have prepared for those who love you such good\par
things as surpass our understanding: Pour into our hearts such\par
love towards you, that we, loving you in all things and above\par
all things, may obtain your promises, which exceed all that we\par
can desire; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\i  Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Easter\i0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday of this week are the traditional\par
Rogation Days.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Ascension Day\b0\par
 \par
Almighty God, whose blessed Son our Savior Jesus Christ\par
ascended far above all heavens that he might fill all things:\par
Mercifully give us faith to perceive that, according to his\par
promise, he abides with his Church on earth, even to the end\par
of the ages; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, in glory\par
everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, we pray, Almighty God, that as we believe your\par
only-begotten Son our Lord Jesus Christ to have ascended\par
into heaven, so we may also in heart and mind there ascend,\par
and with him continually dwell; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Ascension\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 Either of the preceding Collects, with the proper Psalm and Lessons for\par
Ascension Day, serves for the following weekdays, except as otherwise\par
appointed.\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\b Seventh Sunday of Easter:  The Sunday after Ascension Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, the King of glory, you have exalted your only Son\par
Jesus Christ with great triumph to your kingdom in heaven:\par
Do not leave us comfortless, but send us your Holy Spirit to\par
strengthen us, and exalt us to that place where our Savior\par
Christ has gone before; who lives and reigns with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Ascension\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b The Day of Pentecost:  Whitsunday\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 When a Vigil of Pentecost is observed, it begins with the Service of\par
Light, page 109 (substituting, if desired, the Gloria in excelsis for\par
the Phos hilaron), and continues with the Salutation and Collect of the\par
Day.  Three or more of the appointed Lessons are read before the Gospel,\par
each followed by a Psalm, Canticle, or hymn.  Holy Baptism or\par
Confirmation (beginning with the Presentation of the Candidates), or the\par
Renewal of Baptismal Vows, page 292, follows the Sermon.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, on this day you opened the way of eternal life\par
to every race and nation by the promised gift of your Holy\par
Spirit:  Shed abroad this gift throughout the world by the\par
preaching of the Gospel, that it may reach to the ends of the\par
earth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who on this day taught the hearts of your faithful\par
people by sending to them the light of your Holy Spirit:\par
Grant us by the same Spirit to have a right judgment in all\par
things, and evermore to rejoice in his holy comfort; through\par
Jesus Christ your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Pentecost\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 On the weekdays which follow, the numbered Proper which corresponds\par
most closely to the date of Pentecost in that year is used.  See page\par
158.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional summer\par
Ember Days.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\par
\par
\b First Sunday after Pentecost:  Trinity Sunday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, you have given to us\par
your servants grace, by the confession of a true faith, to\par
acknowledge the glory of the eternal Trinity, and in the\par
power of your divine Majesty to worship the Unity:  Keep\par
us steadfast in this faith and worship, and bring us at last to\par
see you in your one and eternal glory, O Father; who with\par
the Son and the Holy Spirit live and reign, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday \par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\fs20 On the weekdays which follow, the numbered Proper which corresponds\par
most closely to the date of Trinity Sunday in that year is used.\i0\par
 \fs24\par
\par
\par
 \par
\fs36 The Season after Pentecost\fs24\par
 \par
\i\fs20 Directions for the use of the Propers which follow are on page 158.\i0\fs24\par
 \par
\b Proper 1\b0   \i\fs20  Week of the Sunday closest to May 11\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Remember, O Lord, what you have wrought in us and not\par
what we deserve; and, as you have called us to your service,\par
make us worthy of our calling; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 No Proper Preface is used.\fs24\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 2\b0    \i\fs20 Week of the Sunday closest to May 18\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and merciful God, in your goodness keep us, we\par
pray, from all things that may hurt us, that we, being ready\par
\par
\par
both in mind and body, may accomplish with free hearts\par
those things which belong to your purpose; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 No Proper Preface is used.\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\b Proper 3\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to May 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, O Lord, that the course of this world may be\par
peaceably governed by your providence; and that your\par
Church may joyfully serve you in confidence and serenity;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 4\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, your never-failing providence sets in order all things\par
both in heaven and earth:  Put away from us, we entreat you,\par
all hurtful things, and give us those things which are profitable\par
for us; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 5\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 8\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, from whom all good proceeds:  Grant that by your\par
inspiration we may think those things that are right, and by\par
your merciful guiding may do them; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\par
\b Proper 6\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 15\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Keep, O Lord, your household the Church in your steadfast\par
faith and love, that through your grace we may proclaim\par
your truth with boldness, and minister your justice with\par
compassion; for the sake of our Savior Jesus Christ, who\par
lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now\par
and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 7\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 22\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Lord, make us have perpetual love and reverence for your\par
holy Name, for you never fail to help and govern those whom\par
you have set upon the sure foundation of your loving-kindness;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 8\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have built your Church upon the\par
foundation of the apostles and prophets, Jesus Christ himself\par
being the chief cornerstone:  Grant us so to be joined together\par
in unity of spirit by their teaching, that we may be made a\par
holy temple acceptable to you; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 9\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you have taught us to keep all your commandments\par
by loving you and our neighbor:  Grant us the grace of your\par
Holy Spirit, that we may be devoted to you with our whole\par
\par
heart, and united to one another with pure affection; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 10\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 13\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O Lord, mercifully receive the prayers of your people who\par
call upon you, and grant that they may know and understand\par
what things they ought to do, and also may have grace and\par
power faithfully to accomplish them; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit,\par
one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 11\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 20\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, the fountain of all wisdom, you know our\par
necessities before we ask and our ignorance in asking:  Have\par
compassion on our weakness, and mercifully give us those\par
things which for our unworthiness we dare not, and for our\par
blindness we cannot ask; through the worthiness of your Son\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 12\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 27\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, the protector of all who trust in you, without whom\par
nothing is strong, nothing is holy:  Increase and multiply upon\par
us your mercy; that, with you as our ruler and guide, we may so\par
pass through things temporal, that we lose not the things eternal; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\b\i0 Proper 13\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 3\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Let your continual mercy, O Lord, cleanse and defend your\par
Church; and, because it cannot continue in safety without\par
your help, protect and govern it always by your goodness;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 14\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 10\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant to us, Lord, we pray, the spirit to think and do always\par
those things that are right, that we, who cannot exist without\par
you, may by you be enabled to live according to your will;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 15\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 17\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have given your only Son to be for us a\par
sacrifice for sin, and also an example of godly life:  Give us\par
grace to receive thankfully the fruits of his redeeming work,\par
and to follow daily in the blessed steps of his most holy life;\par
through Jesus Christ your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 16\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, O merciful God, that your Church, being gathered\par
together in unity by your Holy Spirit, may show forth your\par
power among all peoples, to the glory of your Name;\par
\par
\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirt, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 17\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 31\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord of all power and might, the author and giver of all good\par
things:  Graft in our hearts the love of your Name; increase in\par
us true religion; nourish us with all goodness; and bring forth\par
in us the fruit of good works; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 18\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 7\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant us, O Lord, to trust in you with all our hearts; for, as\par
you always resist the proud who confide in their own strength,\par
so you never forsake those who make their boast of your\par
mercy; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 19\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 14\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, because without you we are not able to please you,\par
mercifully grant that your Holy Spirit may in all things direct\par
and rule our hearts; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 The Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday after September 14 are the\par
traditional autumnal Ember Days.\i0\fs24\par
 \b Proper 20\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Grant us, Lord, not to be anxious about earthly things, but to\par
love things heavenly; and even now, while we are placed among things that are passing away, to hold fast to those that shall\par
endure; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
 \par
\b Proper 21\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you declare your almighty power chiefly in showing\par
mercy and pity:  Grant us the fullness of your grace, that we,\par
running to obtain your promises, may become partakers of\par
your heavenly treasure; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who\par
lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for\par
ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 22\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 5\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, you are always more ready to\par
hear than we to pray, and to give more than we either desire\par
or deserve:  Pour upon us the abundance of your mercy,\par
forgiving us those things of which our conscience is afraid,\par
and giving us those good things for which we are not worthy\par
to ask, except through the merits and mediation of Jesus\par
Christ our Savior; who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 23\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 12\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord, we pray that your grace may always precede and\par
follow us, that we may continually be given to good works;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 24\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 19\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, in Christ you have revealed\par
your glory among the nations:  Preserve the works of your\par
mercy, that your Church throughout the world may\par
persevere with steadfast faith in the confession of your\par
Name; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 25\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 26\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, increase in us the gifts of\par
faith, hope, and charity; and, that we may obtain what you\par
promise, make us love what you command; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
 \i0  \par
\b Proper 26\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 2\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and merciful God, it is only by your gift that your\par
faithful people offer you true and laudable service:  Grant\par
that we may run without stumbling to obtain your heavenly\par
promises; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\par
\i0  \par
\par
\b Proper 27\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 9\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, whose blessed Son came into the world that he might\par
destroy the works of the devil and make us children of God\par
and heirs of eternal life:  Grant that, having this hope, we may\par
purify ourselves as he is pure; that, when he comes again\par
with power and great glory, we may be made like him in his\par
eternal and glorious kingdom; where he lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 28\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 16\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Blessed Lord, who caused all holy Scriptures to be written for\par
our learning: Grant us so to hear them, read, mark, learn,\par
and inwardly digest them, that we may embrace and ever\par
hold fast the blessed hope of everlasting life, which you have\par
given us in our Savior Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
  \par
\b Proper 29\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 23\i0\fs24\par
 \par
Almighty and everlasting God, whose will it is to restore all\par
things in your well-beloved Son, the King of kings and Lord of\par
lords:  Mercifully grant that the peoples of the earth, divided\par
and enslaved by sin, may be freed and brought together\par
under his most gracious rule; who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day, or of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\fs36 Holy Days\fs24\par
\par
\par
\b Saint Andrew\b0    \i\fs20 November 30\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Almighty God, who gave such grace to your apostle Andrew\par
that he readily obeyed the call of your Son Jesus Christ, and\par
brought his brother with him: Give us, who are called by\par
your holy Word, grace to follow him without delay, and to\par
bring those near to us into his gracious presence; who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Thomas\b0    \i\fs20 December 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Everliving God, who strengthened your apostle Thomas with\par
firm and certain faith in your Son\rquote s resurrection: Grant us so\par
perfectly and without doubt to believe in Jesus Christ, our\par
Lord and our God, that our faith may never be found wanting\par
in your sight; through him who lives and reigns with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\par
 \i0  \par
\b Saint Stephen\b0    \i\fs20 December 26\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard We give you thanks, O Lord of glory, for the example of\par
the first martyr Stephen, who looked up to heaven and prayed\par
for his persecutors to your Son Jesus Christ, who stands at\par
your right hand; where he lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b Saint John\b0    \i\fs20 December 27\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Shed upon your Church, O Lord, the brightness of your light,\par
that we, being illumined by the teaching of your apostle and\par
evangelist John, may so walk in the light of your truth, that\par
at length we may attain to the fullness of eternal life; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
  \par
\b The Holy Innocents\b0   \i\fs20 December 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard We remember today, O God, the slaughter of the holy\par
innocents of Bethlehem by King Herod. Receive, we pray,\par
into the arms of your mercy all innocent victims; and by your\par
great might frustrate the designs of evil tyrants and establish\par
your rule of justice, love, and peace; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the\par
Holy Spirit,, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\par
 \i0  \par
\b Confession of Saint Peter\b0    \i\fs20 January 18\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty Father, who inspired Simon Peter, first among the\par
apostles, to confess Jesus as Messiah and Son of the living God:\par
Keep your Church steadfast upon the rock of this faith, so that\par
in unity and peace we may proclaim the one truth and follow\par
the one Lord, our Savior Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \par
\b Conversion of Saint Paul \b0   \i\fs20 January 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, by the preaching of your apostle Paul you have\par
caused the light of the Gospel to shine throughout the world:\par
\par
Grant, we pray, that we, having his wonderful conversion in\par
remembrance, may show ourselves thankful to you by following\par
his holy teaching; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\par
 \i0  \par
\b The Presentation\b0    \i\fs20 February 2\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everliving God, we humbly pray that, as your\par
only-begotten Son was this day presented in the temple, so\par
we may be presented to you with pure and clean hearts by\par
Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Matthias\b0    \i\fs20 February 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, who in the place of Judas chose your faithful\par
servant Matthias to be numbered among the Twelve: Grant that\par
your Church, being delivered from false apostles, may always\par
be guided and governed by faithful and true pastors; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the\par
unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Joseph\b0    \i\fs20 March 19\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who from the family of your servant David raised\par
up Joseph to be the guardian of your incarnate Son and the\par
spouse of his virgin mother: Give us grace to imitate his\par
uprightness of life and his obedience to your commands;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\b The Annunciation\b0    \i\fs20 March 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Pour your grace into our hearts, O Lord, that we who have\par
known the incarnation of your Son Jesus Christ, announced\par
by an angel to the Virgin Mary, may by his cross and passion\par
be brought to the glory of his resurrection; who lives and\par
reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now\par
and for ever  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\pard\sl156\slmult1   \par
\pard\b Saint Mark\b0    \i\fs20 April 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, by the hand of Mark the evangelist you have\par
given to your Church the Gospel of Jesus Christ the Son of\par
God: We thank you for this witness, and pray that we may be\par
firmly grounded in its truth; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\pard\sl156\slmult1   \par
\pard\b Saint Philip and Saint James\b0    \i\fs20 May 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, who gave to your apostles Philip and James grace and strength to bear witness to the truth: Grant that we, being mindful of their victory of faith, may glorify in life and death the Name of our Lord Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\pard\sl156\slmult1   \par
\pard\b The Visitation\b0   \i\fs20 May 31\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Father in heaven, by your grace the virgin mother of your\par
incarnate Son was blessed in bearing him, but still more\par
blessed in keeping your word: Grant us who honor the\par
exaltation of her lowliness to follow the example of her\par
devotion to your will; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who\par
lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for\par
ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl72\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Barnabas\b0    \i\fs20 June 11\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, O God, that we may follow the example of your\par
faithful servant Barnabas, who, seeking not his own renown\par
but the well-being of your Church, gave generously of his\par
life and substance for the relief of the poor and the spread\par
of the Gospel; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl72\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\par
 \i0  \par
\b The Nativity of Saint John the Baptist\b0    \i\fs20 June 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, by whose providence your servant John the\par
Baptist was wonderfully born, and sent to prepare the way of\par
your Son our Savior by preaching repentance: Make us so to\par
follow his teaching and holy life, that we may truly repent\par
according to his preaching; and, following his example,\par
constantly speak the truth, boldly rebuke vice, and patiently\par
suffer for the truth\rquote s sake; through Jesus Christ your Son our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl72\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Advent\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Peter and Saint Paul\b0    \i\fs20 June 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose blessed apostles Peter and Paul glorified\par
you by their martyrdom: Grant that your Church, instructed by\par
their teaching and example, and knit together in unity by your\par
Spirit, may ever stand firm upon the one foundation, which\par
is Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with you, in the\par
unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl72\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Independence Day\b0    \i\fs20 July 4\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord God Almighty, in whose Name the founders of this\par
country won liberty for themselves and for us, and lit the\par
torch of freedom for nations then unborn:  Grant that we and\par
all the people of this land may have grace to maintain our\par
liberties in righteousness and peace; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 The Collect \ldblquote For the Nation,\rdblquote  page 258, may be used instead.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\fs24  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\par
 \i0  \par
\b Saint Mary Magdalene\b0    \i\fs20 July 22\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose blessed Son restored Mary Magdalene\par
to health of body and of mind, and called her to be a witness\par
of his resurrection:  Mercifully grant that by your grace we\par
may be healed from all our infirmities and know you in the power of his unending life; who with you and the Holy Spirit\par
lives and reigns, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\par
\b Saint James\b0    \i\fs20 July 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard O gracious God, we remember before you today your servant\par
and apostle James, first among the Twelve to suffer martyrdom\par
for the Name of Jesus Christ; and we pray that you will pour\par
out upon the leaders of your Church that spirit of self-denying\par
service by which alone they may have true authority among\par
your people; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \b\par
The Transfiguration\b0    \i\fs20 August 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who on the holy mount revealed to chosen witnesses\par
your well-beloved Son, wonderfully transfigured, in raiment\par
white and glistening:  Mercifully grant that we, being\par
delivered from the disquietude of this world, may by faith\par
behold the King in his beauty; who with you, O Father, and\par
you, O Holy Spirit, lives and reigns, one God, for ever and\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Mary the Virgin\b0   \i\fs20 August 15\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you have taken to yourself the blessed Virgin Mary,\par
mother of your incarnate Son:  Grant that we, who have been\par
redeemed by his blood, may share with her the glory of your\par
eternal kingdom; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives\par
and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Incarnation\par
 \i0  \par
\b Saint Bartholomew\b0    \i\fs20 August 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, who gave to your apostle\par
Bartholomew grace truly to believe and to preach your\par
Word:  Grant that your Church may love what he believed\par
and preach what he taught; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\par
 \i0\par
\par
\b Holy Cross Day\b0    \i\fs20 September 14\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose Son our Savior Jesus Christ was lifted\par
high upon the cross that he might draw the whole world to\par
himself:  Mercifully grant that we, who glory in the mystery\par
of our redemption, may have grace to take up our cross and\par
follow him; who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Matthew\b0    \i\fs20 September 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard We thank you, heavenly Father, for the witness of your apostle\par
and evangelist Matthew to the Gospel of your Son our Savior;\par
and we pray that, after his example, we may with ready wills\par
and hearts obey the calling of our Lord to follow him;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Michael and All Angels\b0    \i\fs20 September 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Everlasting God, you have ordained and constituted in a\par
wonderful order the ministries of angels and mortals:\par
Mercifully grant that, as your holy angels always serve and\par
worship you in heaven, so by your appointment they may\par
help and defend us here on earth; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Luke\b0   \i\fs20 October 18\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, who inspired your servant Luke the physician\par
to set forth in the Gospel the love and healing power of your\par
Son:  Graciously continue in your Church this love and power\par
to heal, to the praise and glory of your Name; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity\par
of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of All Saints\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint James of Jerusalem\b0    \i\fs20 October 23\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, O God, that, following the example of your servant\par
James the Just, brother of our Lord, your Church may give\par
itself continually to prayer and to the reconciliation of all\par
who are at variance and enmity; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of All Saints\i0\par
  \par
\b Saint Simon and Saint Jude\b0    \i\fs20 October 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard O God, we thank you for the glorious company of the apostles,\par
and especially on this day for Simon and Jude; and we pray\par
that, as they were faithful and zealous in their mission, so we\par
may with ardent devotion make known the love and mercy of\par
our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
  \par
\b All Saints\rquote  Day\b0    \i\fs20 November 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have knit together your elect in one\par
communion and fellowship in the mystical body of your Son\par
Christ our Lord:  Give us grace so to follow your blessed saints\par
in all virtuous and godly living, that we may come to those\par
ineffable joys that you have prepared for those who truly love\par
you; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who with you and the Holy\par
Spirit lives and reigns, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\b Thanksgiving Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and gracious Father, we give you thanks for the\par
fruits of the earth in their season and for the labors of those\par
who harvest them.  Make us, we pray, faithful stewards of\par
your great bounty, for the provision of our necessities and\par
the relief of all who are in need, to the glory of your Name;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 For the Prayers of the People, the Litany of Thanksgiving on page 836\par
may be used.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
 \par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\fs36 The Common of Saints\fs24\par
 \par
\par
\i\fs20 The festival of a saint is observed in accordance with the rules of\par
precedence set forth in the Calendar of the Church Year.\par
 \par
At the discretion of the Celebrant, and as appropriate, any of the\par
following Collects, with one of the corresponding sets of Psalms and\par
Lessons, may be used\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard a) at the commemoration of a saint listed in the Calendar for which no\par
Proper is provided in this Book\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard b) at the patronal festival or commemoration of a saint not listed in\par
the Calendar.\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\b Of a Martyr\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, who gave to your servant \i N\i0 . boldness to\par
confess the Name of our Savior Jesus Christ before the rulers\par
of this world, and courage to die for this faith:  Grant that we\par
may always be ready to give a reason for the hope that is in\par
us, and to suffer gladly for the sake of our Lord Jesus Christ;\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, by whose grace and power your holy martyr\par
\i N\i0 . triumphed over suffering and was faithful even to death:\par
Grant us, who now remember \i him\i0  in thanksgiving, to be so\par
faithful in our witness to you in this world, that we may\par
receive with \i him\i0  the crown of life; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, who kindled the flame of your\par
love in the heart of your holy martyr \i N\i0 .:  Grant to us, your\par
humble servants, a like faith and power of love, that we who\par
rejoice in \i her\i0  triumph may profit by \i her\i0  example; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of a Saint\i0\par
  \par
\b Of a Missionary\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, we thank you for your\par
servant \i N\i0 ., whom you called to preach the Gospel to the\par
people of_________. (\i or\i0  to the__________. people).  Raise\par
up in this and every land evangelists and heralds of your\par
kingdom, that your Church may proclaim the unsearchable\par
riches of our Savior Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or the following\i0\fs24  \par
 \par
Almighty God, whose will it is to be glorified in your saints,\par
and who raised up your servant \i N\i0 . to be a light in the world:\par
Shine, we pray, in our hearts, that we also in our generation\par
may show forth your praise, who called us out of darkness\par
into your marvelous light; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Pentecost\i0\par
\par
\b Of a Pastor\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Heavenly Father, Shepherd of your people, we thank you for\par
your servant \i N\i0 ., who was faithful in the care and nurture of\par
your flock; and we pray that, following \i his\i0  example and the\par
teaching of \i his\i0  holy life, we may by your grace grow into the\par
stature of the fullness of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ;\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, our heavenly Father, who raised up your faithful\par
servant \i N\i0 ., to be a [bishop and] pastor in your Church and to\par
feed your flock:  Give abundantly to all pastors the gifts of\par
your Holy Spirit, that they may minister in your household as\par
true servants of Christ and stewards of your divine mysteries;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of a Saint\i0\par
 \par
\b Of a Theologian and Teacher\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, by your Holy Spirit you give to some the word of\par
wisdom, to others the word of knowledge, and to others the\par
word of faith:  We praise your Name for the gifts of grace\par
manifested in your servant \i N\i0 ., and we pray that your Church\par
may never be destitute of such gifts; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who with you and the Holy Spirit lives and reigns, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you gave to your servant \i N\i0 . special gifts of\par
grace to understand and teach the truth as it is in Christ Jesus:\par
Grant that by this teaching we may know you, the one true\par
God, and Jesus Christ whom you have sent; who lives and\par
reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of a Saint, or of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
  \par
\b Of a Monastic\b0\par
 \par
O God, whose blessed Son became poor that we through his\par
poverty might be rich:  Deliver us from an inordinate love of\par
this world, that we, inspired by the devotion of your servant\par
\i N\i0 ., may serve you with singleness of heart, and attain to the\par
riches of the age to come; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who\par
lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, by whose grace your servant \i N\i0 ., kindled with the\par
flame of your love, became a burning and a shining light in\par
your Church:  Grant that we also may be aflame with the spirit\par
of love and discipline, and walk before you as children of light;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you,\par
in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of a Saint\i0\par
  \par
\b Of a Saint\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have surrounded us with a great cloud of\par
witnesses:  Grant that we, encouraged by the good example of\par
your servant \i N\i0 ., may persevere in running the race that is set\par
before us, until at last we may with \i him\i0  attain to your eternal\par
joy; through Jesus Christ, the pioneer and perfecter of our\par
faith, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\par
\pard O God, you have brought us near to an innumerable company\par
of angels, and to the spirits of just men made perfect:  Grant us\par
during our earthly pilgrimage to abide in their fellowship, and\par
in our heavenly country to become partakers of their joy;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, by your Holy Spirit you have made us one with\par
your saints in heaven and on earth:  Grant that in our earthly\par
pilgrimage we may always be supported by this fellowship of\par
love and prayer, and know ourselves to be surrounded by their\par
witness to your power and mercy.  We ask this for the sake of\par
Jesus Christ, in whom all our intercessions are acceptable\par
through the Spirit, and who lives and reigns for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of a Saint\i0\par
 \par
\par
\fs36 Various Occasions\fs24\par
 \par
\par
\i\fs20 For optional use, when desired, subject to the rules set forth in the\par
Calendar of the Church Year.\i0\fs24\par
  \par
\b 1. Of the Holy Trinity\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have revealed to your Church your eternal\par
Being of glorious majesty and perfect love as one God in\par
Trinity of Persons:  Give us grace to continue steadfast in the\par
confession of this faith, and constant in our worship of you,\par
Father, Son, and Holy Spirit; for you live and reign, one God,\par
now and for ever. \i Amen\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\b 2. Of the Holy Spirit\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and most merciful God, grant that by the indwelling\par
of your Holy Spirit we may be enlightened and strengthened\par
for your service; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now\par
and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Pentecost\i0\par
  \par
\b 3. Of the Holy Angels\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Everlasting God, you have ordained and constituted in a\par
wonderful order the ministries of angels and mortals:\par
Mercifully grant that, as your holy angels always serve and\par
worship you in heaven, so by your appointment they may\par
help and defend us here on earth; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\b 4. Of the Incarnation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, who wonderfully created, and yet more wonderfully\par
restored, the dignity of human nature:  Grant that we may\par
share the divine life of him who humbled himself to share our\par
humanity, your Son Jesus Christ; who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
  \par
\b 5.  Of the Holy Eucharist\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Thursdays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard God our Father, whose Son our Lord Jesus Christ in a\par
wonderful Sacrament has left us a memorial of his passion:\par
Grant us so to venerate the sacred mysteries of his Body and\par
Blood, that we may ever perceive within ourselves the fruit\par
of his redemption; who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
  \par
\b 6. Of the Holy Cross\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Fridays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose beloved Son willingly endured the agony\par
and shame of the cross for our redemption:  Give us courage to\par
take up our cross and follow him; who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
  \par
\b 7. For all Baptized Christians\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Saturdays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, Lord God, to all who have been baptized into the\par
death and resurrection of your Son Jesus Christ, that, as we\par
have put away the old life of sin, so we may be renewed in the\par
spirit of our minds, and live in righteousness and true holiness;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you,\par
in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Baptism\i0\par
  \par
\b 8. For the Departed\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Eternal Lord God, you hold all souls in life:  Give to your\par
whole Church in paradise and on earth your light and your\par
peace; and grant that we, following the good examples of\par
those who have served you here and are now at rest, may at\par
the last enter with them into your unending joy; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the\par
unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, we remember before you today your faithful\par
servant \i N\i0 .; and we pray that, having opened to \i him\i0  the gates\par
of larger life, you will receive \i him\i0  more and more into your\par
joyful service, that, with all who have faithfully served you in\par
the past, \i he\i0  may share in the eternal victory of Jesus Christ\par
our Lord; who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 Any of the Collects appointed for use at the Burial of the Dead may be\par
used instead.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard For the Prayers of the People, one of the forms appointed for the\par
Burial of the Dead may be used.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Commemoration of the Dead\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 The postcommunion prayer on page 498 may be used.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\b 9. Of the Reign of Christ\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, whose will it is to restore all\par
things in your well-beloved Son, the King of kings and Lord\par
of lords:  Mercifully grant that the peoples of the earth,\par
divided and enslaved by sin, may be freed and brought together\par
under his most gracious rule; who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Ascension, or of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\b 10. At Baptism\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Almighty God, by our baptism into the death and resurrection\par
of your Son Jesus Christ, you turn us from the old life of sin:\par
Grant that we, being reborn to new life in him, may live in\par
righteousness and holiness all our days; through Jesus Christ\par
our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit,\par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Baptism\i0\par
  \par
\b 11. At Confirmation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Grant, Almighty God, that we, who have been redeemed\par
from the old life of sin by our baptism into the death and\par
resurrection of your Son Jesus Christ, may be renewed in\par
your Holy Spirit, and live in righteousness and true holiness;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you\par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Baptism, or of Pentecost\i0\par
  \par
\b 12. On the Anniversary of the Dedication of a Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, to whose glory we celebrate the dedication of\par
this house of prayer:  We give you thanks for the fellowship\par
\par
of those who have worshiped in this place, and we pray that\par
all who seek you here may find you, and be filled with your\par
joy and peace; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and\par
reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now\par
and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 The Litany of Thanksgiving for a Church, page 578, may be used for the\par
Prayers of the People.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Dedication of a Church\i0\par
  \par
\b 13.  For a Church Convention\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting Father, you have given the Holy\par
Spirit to abide with us for ever:  Bless, we pray, with his grace\par
and presence, the bishops and the other clergy and the laity\par
here (\i or\i0  now, \i or\i0  soon to be) assembled in your Name, that\par
your Church, being preserved in true faith and godly\par
discipline, may fulfill all the mind of him who loved it and\par
gave himself for it, your Son Jesus Christ our Savior; who\par
lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Pentecost, or of the Season\par
 \i0  \par
\b 14.  For the Unity of the Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty Father, whose blessed Son before his passion prayed\par
for his disciples that they might be one, as you and he are one:\par
Grant that your Church, being bound together in love and\par
obedience to you, may be united in one body by the one Spirit,\par
that the world may believe in him whom you have sent, your\par
Son Jesus Christ our Lord; who lives and reigns with you, in\par
the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Baptism, or of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
 \par
\b 15.  For the Ministry (Ember Days)\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\i\fs20 For use on the traditional days or at other times\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard I.  For those to be ordained\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, the giver of all good gifts, in your divine\par
providence you have appointed various orders in your\par
Church:  Give your grace, we humbly pray, to all who are\par
[now] called to any office and ministry for your people; and so\par
fill them with the truth of your doctrine and clothe them with\par
holiness of life, that they may faithfully serve before you, to\par
the glory of your great Name and for the benefit of your holy\par
Church; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Apostles\i0\par
 \par
\i II.  For the choice of fit persons for the ministry\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you led your holy apostles to ordain ministers in every\par
place:  Grant that your Church, under the guidance of the Holy Spirit, may choose suitable persons for the ministry of Word and Sacrament, and may uphold them in their work for the extension of your kingdom; through him who is the Shepherd and Bishop of our souls, Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\par
 \i0  \par
\i III. For all Christians in their vocation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty and everlasting God, by whose Spirit the whole\par
body of your faithful people is governed and sanctified:\par
Receive our supplications and prayers, which we offer before\par
\par
you for all members of your holy Church, that in their vocation and ministry they may truly and devoutly serve you; through our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of Baptism, or of the Season\i0\par
  \par
\b 16. For the Mission of the Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God, you have made of one blood all the peoples of the\par
earth, and sent your blessed Son to preach peace to those\par
who are far off and to those who are near:  Grant that people\par
everywhere may seek after you and find you, bring the nations\par
into your fold, pour out your Spirit upon all flesh, and hasten\par
the coming of your kingdom; through Jesus Christ our Lord,\par
who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God,\par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard O God of all the nations of the earth:  Remember the\par
multitudes who have been created in your image but have not\par
known the redeeming work of our Savior Jesus Christ; and\par
grant that, by the prayers and labors of your holy Church,\par
they may be brought to know and worship you as you have\par
been revealed in your Son; who lives and reigns with you and\par
the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season, or of Pentecost\par
 \i0\par
\par
\b 17. For the Nation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Lord God Almighty, you have made all the peoples of the\par
earth for your glory, to serve you in freedom and in peace:\par
Give to the people of our country a zeal for justice and the\par
strength of forbearance, that we may use our liberty in\par
accordance with your gracious will; through Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\fs20 The Collect for Independence Day may be used instead.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\fs24  \par
\pard Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
  \par
\b 18. For Peace\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, kindle, we pray, in every heart the true love of\par
peace, and guide with your wisdom those who take counsel\par
for the nations of the earth, that in tranquillity your dominion\par
may increase until the earth is filled with the knowledge of your love; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\par
 \i0  \par
\b 19. For Rogation Days\b0\par
 \par
\i\fs20 For use on the traditional days or at other times\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard I. For fruitful seasons\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, Lord of heaven and earth: We humbly pray\par
that your gracious providence may give and preserve to our\par
use the harvests of the land and of the seas, and may prosper\par
all who labor to gather them, that we, who are constantly\par
receiving good things from your hand, may always give you\par
\par
\par
thanks; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
 \par
\i II. For commerce and industry\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, whose Son Jesus Christ in his earthly life\par
shared our toil and hallowed our labor:  Be present with your\par
people where they work; make those who carry on the industries\par
and commerce of this land responsive to your will; and give\par
to us all a pride in what we do, and a just return for our labor;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for\par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\par
 \par
III. For stewardship of creation\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \i0\par
\pard O merciful Creator, your hand is open wide to satisfy the\par
needs of every living creature:  Make us always thankful for\par
your loving providence; and grant that we, remembering the\par
account that we must one day give, may be faithful stewards\par
of your good gifts; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who with\par
you and the Holy Spirit lives and reigns, one God, for ever\par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
 \par
\par
\b 20. For the Sick\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Heavenly Father, giver of life and health: Comfort and\par
relieve your sick servants, and give your power of healing to\par
those who minister to their needs, that those (\i or\i0  \i N., or\i0  \i NN\i0 .)\par
for whom our prayers are offered may be strengthened in\par
\i their\i0  weakness and have confidence in your loving care;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with\par
you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Season\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\fs20 The postcommunion prayer on page 457 may be used.\i0\par
\fs24\par
\b 21. For Social Justice\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, who created us in your own image: Grant us\par
grace fearlessly to contend against evil and to make no peace\par
with oppression; and, that we may reverently use our freedom,\par
help us to employ it in the maintenance of justice in our\par
communities and among the nations, to the glory of your holy\par
Name; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
  \par
\b 22. For Social Service\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Heavenly Father, whose blessed Son came not to be served\par
but to serve: Bless all who, following in his steps, give\par
themselves to the service of others; that with wisdom,\par
patience, and courage, they may minister in his Name to the\par
suffering, the friendless, and the needy for the love of him\par
who laid down his life for us, your Son our Savior Jesus\par
Christ, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit,\par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
\b\par
23. For Education\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, the fountain of all wisdom:  Enlighten by your\par
Holy Spirit those who teach and those who learn, that,\par
rejoicing in the knowledge of your truth, they may worship\par
you and serve you from generation to generation; through\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
  \par
\b 24. For Vocation in Daily Work\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God our heavenly Father, you declare your glory\par
and show forth your handiwork in the heavens and in the\par
earth:  Deliver us in our various occupations from the service\par
of self alone, that we may do the work you give us to do in\par
truth and beauty and for the common good; for the sake of\par
him who came among us as one who serves, your Son Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard Preface of the Season \i0\par
 \par
\b 25. For Labor Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Almighty God, you have so linked our lives one with another\par
that all we do affects, for good or ill, all other lives:  So guide\par
us in the work we do, that we may do it not for self alone, but\par
for the common good; and, as we seek a proper return for\par
our own labor, make us mindful of the rightful aspirations of\par
other workers, and arouse our concern for those who are out\par
of work; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns\par
with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.\par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard Preface of the Season\i0\par
 \par
}
